@bank all
// Pillar 5 Step 4 (head writer W2): texts said by nobody, for the side jobs (seats E1, E2, E3; D3's pages on
// claude/p5-design). Keys in content/works/keys-p5.md, "Step 4". Mails are "Subject | body", unsigned.

// ---- the ladder rows
== works.mech.m10
- the workshop
== works.mech.m11
- tool upkeep
== works.mech.m12
- the logbook
== works.mech.m13
- leak hunting
== works.mech.m14
- irrigation
== works.mech.m15
- rewiring
== works.mech.m17
- the lift roof
== works.mech.tickets
- fault-finder tickets

// ---- M10 the workshop (E3, 24j; E3's names): an order's ask (said by the crew member, on the order card) and their
// thanks when you hand it over ({name} is them), per thing id; a quiet Mail when an order sat a week untaken.
== works.order.ask.guitar-hook
- A hook for my guitar, please. It keeps sliding off the bunk.
== works.order.thanks.guitar-hook
- A guitar hook! It hasn't fallen once. Thank you.
== works.order.ask.mug-rack
- A little rack for mugs? Ours are stacked like a tower.
== works.order.thanks.mug-rack
- The mug rack's perfect. The tower is no more.
== works.order.ask.book-stand
- A stand for my book, please. My arms get tired reading.
== works.order.thanks.book-stand
- A book stand! I read two chapters hands-free. Thank you.
== works.order.ask.lamp-arm
- Could you make an arm for my lamp? It lights the wall, not the page.
== works.order.thanks.lamp-arm
- The lamp arm works. I can see my page. Thank you.
== works.order.ask.plant-hanger
- A hanger for my plant? It wants to be nearer the light.
== works.order.thanks.plant-hanger
- The plant's up and happy. So am I. Thank you.
== works.order.ask.fan-spindle
- My desk fan's spindle snapped. Could you turn me a new one?
== works.order.thanks.fan-spindle
- The fan spins again. Better than new, honestly.
== works.order.ask.drawer-pull
- My drawer's lost its pull. I open it with a spoon.
== works.order.thanks.drawer-pull
- A proper drawer pull. Goodbye, spoon. Thank you.
== works.order.ask.tablet-stand
- A stand for my reader, please. I keep propping it on socks.
== works.order.thanks.tablet-stand
- The stand's lovely. My socks are free again. Thanks.
== works.order.lapse
- I made do, don't worry. Thanks anyway.

// ---- M11 tool upkeep (E1, 24m)
== works.toolstate.charged
- Charged
== works.toolstate.low
- Getting low
== works.toolstate.due
- Due
== tool.due.scanner
- Your scanner's charge is low. The bench will sort it.
== tool.due.pipekit
- Your pipe kit wants cleaning and a new seal. Bench, when you can.
== tool.due.logger
- Your logger's due a check. Bench, when you can.
== bench.scanner
- Recharge the scanner
== bench.pipekit
- Clean and re-seal the pipe kit
== bench.logger
- Check the logger
== bench.charging
- The scanner's on charge. Ready at {time}. No need to wait.
== bench.charging.now
- on charge
== bench.rack
- The team's tools
== bench.rack.done
- Rack's tidy. Someone's been busy.
== bench.done
- Good as new. Well, good as yesterday.

// ---- M12 the logbook (E1, 24n): the terminal, workdays 16:30-17:30. You pick one of three summaries; E1 builds them
// from these parts and joins them with "; ".
== works.log.write
- Write the log
== works.log.pick
- Which one's your log for today?
== log.fixed
- {machine}: {part} replaced
== log.serviced
- {machine} serviced
== log.found
- {machine} {shows}, left for tomorrow
== log.open
- {machine} still open
== log.quiet
- A quiet day. Nothing to report
== log.saved
- Logged. Calder will read it. She reads everything.
// stage 2: flag a machine for the night crew's 22:00 look
== log.flag
- Flag {machine} for the night crew
== log.flagged
- Flagged. The night crew will look at 22:00.
// stage 3: your old log line as a clue in a head-scratcher
== case.log.note
- From your log, day {n}: "{text}"

// ---- M13 leak hunting (E2, 24o)
== leak.card
- A pipe drips somewhere on Deck {deck}
== leak.look.above
- It's coming from above, towards {place}.
== leak.look.warmer
- Wetter here. You're close.
== leak.look.here
- There. A joint, weeping.
== leak.worn
- Worn right through. Tightening won't hold it. It needs a new joint from stores.
== leak.turning
- A quarter turn. Still a bead of water. A bit more.
== leak.tight
- Snug. The drip stops.
== leak.fix.tighten
- Tighten the joint
== leak.fix.replace
- Replace the joint ({part})
== leak.done
- Dry. Found it yourself.
== leak.found.crew
- The crew found the drip on Deck {deck}. The long way.

// ---- M14 irrigation (E2, 24r): harvest mornings, the garden's three racks
== noz.plant
- The irrigation plant hums along. You check its filter and the pressure while you're here.
== irr.title
- Rack {n} · nozzles
== irr.clear
- Clear the nozzles
== irr.cleared
- Clear. The water runs even again.
== irr.flush
- Flush the line
== irr.flushed
- Flushed. The racks drink properly now.
== irr.salad
- Tonight's salad is extra crunchy. The garden says thank you.

// ---- M15 rewiring (E2, 24q)
== rewire.card
- Rewire junction {junction}
== rewire.pop
- Pop. That pair's wrong. Swap them and try again.
== rewire.right
- Right first time.
== rewire.done
- Junction {junction} rewired. Lights steady.
== rewire.faded
- This one's faded. Which colour was it?
== rewire.check
- Flick the lights. See which one goes off.
== wire.red
- red
== wire.blue
- blue
== wire.yellow
- yellow
== wire.green
- green
== wire.white
- white
== wire.black
- black

// ---- favour cases (E2, 24l): six small mysteries a friend brings you. Each: the ask (chat, or Mail), the Fault
// notes title, suspects (sus.1 is the real one), clues, the solve line, the thanks. Gifts are E2's.
== favour.lamp.ask
- My lamp flickers, but only when Pell plays guitar next door. Is that mad?
== mail.favour.lamp
- My lamp | My lamp flickers, but only when Pell plays his guitar next door. Is that mad? Could you have a look?
== favour.lamp.title
- A lamp that flickers when the guitar plays
== favour.lamp.sus.1
- they share a circuit, and the amp pulls hard
== favour.lamp.sus.2
- a loose bulb
== favour.lamp.sus.3
- the lamp's switch is worn
== favour.lamp.clue.1
- New bulb, seated tight. Still flickers.
== favour.lamp.clue.2
- Pell: "I only plug the amp in for the loud ones."
== favour.lamp.clue.3
- Both cabins come off the same junction.
== favour.lamp.solved
- Shared circuit. The amp on the other socket, and the lamp's steady.

== favour.cold.ask
- My cabin's freezing, and nobody else's is. Is it me?
== mail.favour.cold
- Cold cabin | My cabin's freezing and nobody else's is. The heating's on, I checked. Could you look?
== favour.cold.title
- A cabin colder than its neighbours
== favour.cold.sus.1
- something's blocking the vent
== favour.cold.sus.2
- the heat loop's low
== favour.cold.sus.3
- a draught at the door
== favour.cold.clue.1
- The cabins either side are warm. Same loop.
== favour.cold.clue.2
- No draught at the door. You checked with your hand.
== favour.cold.clue.3
- A storage box sits snug against the wall, low down.
== favour.cold.solved
- The box was over the vent. Moved it. Warm in ten minutes.

== favour.squeak.ask
- My door squeaks. Only at night. I'm not imagining it.
== mail.favour.squeak
- My door | My door squeaks, but only at night. In the day it's silent. Am I imagining it?
== favour.squeak.title
- A door that only squeaks at night
== favour.squeak.sus.1
- the frame cools at night and the door rubs
== favour.squeak.sus.2
- the hinge wants oil
== favour.squeak.sus.3
- someone leans on it
== favour.squeak.clue.1
- Oiled the hinge yesterday, they say. Still squeaks at night.
== favour.squeak.clue.2
- The corridor's two degrees cooler after 22:00.
== favour.squeak.clue.3
- A shiny rubbed spot near the top of the frame.
== favour.squeak.solved
- The frame shrinks in the cool. A shave off the top, and it's quiet.

== favour.shower.ask
- My shower goes cold. But only when the laundry's running. Weird?
== mail.favour.shower
- Cold shower | My shower goes cold, but only when the laundry's running. Is that a thing?
== favour.shower.title
- A shower that runs cold when the laundry runs
== favour.shower.sus.1
- the shower and the washers share a line
== favour.shower.sus.2
- the shower's mixer is worn
== favour.shower.sus.3
- the water's low ship-wide
== favour.shower.clue.1
- Fine at 07:00. Cold at 11:00, when the washers fill.
== favour.shower.clue.2
- The next shower along is fine all day.
== favour.shower.clue.3
- One pipe feeds this shower and the laundry, by the map.
== favour.shower.solved
- A shared line. A balancing valve in, and the shower keeps its heat.

== favour.clock.ask
- My clock runs slow. A few minutes a day. I'm always late.
== mail.favour.clock
- My clock | My clock loses a few minutes every day. I've been late twice. Could you take a look?
== favour.clock.title
- A clock that runs slow
== favour.clock.sus.1
- the power dips on that circuit
== favour.clock.sus.2
- the clock's tired
== favour.clock.sus.3
- someone keeps setting it wrong
== favour.clock.clue.1
- The same clock ran fine in the mess for a day.
== favour.clock.clue.2
- The lights in that cabin dim when the heater kicks in.
== favour.clock.clue.3
- Nobody else touches it. They'd know.
== favour.clock.solved
- Power dips. A steadier socket, and the clock keeps time.

== favour.speaker.ask
- My speaker buzzes. Only near the scrubber. Can you help?
== mail.favour.speaker
- My speaker | My little speaker buzzes, but only when I'm near the scrubber. Elsewhere it's fine. Any ideas?
== favour.speaker.title
- A speaker that buzzes near the scrubber
== favour.speaker.sus.1
- the scrubber's motor makes interference
== favour.speaker.sus.2
- the speaker's cone is torn
== favour.speaker.sus.3
- a loose cable
== favour.speaker.clue.1
- It plays clean in the common room.
== favour.speaker.clue.2
- The buzz rises and falls with the scrubber's fan.
== favour.speaker.clue.3
- The cable's snug at both ends.
== favour.speaker.solved
- Interference. Moved it a metre away, and the buzz is gone.

// choosing the cause, and a wrong pick (E2)
== favour.call
- What's causing it?
== favour.not
- Not that. Look again.
// the lapse, after 3 days: they ask someone else (the game adds who)
== favour.lapse
- {name} asked someone else in the end. No harm done.
// the Fault notes heading for a favour
== favour.head
- A favour for {name}

// ---- fault-finder tickets (E2): Calder's Mail (Day 13), the Works board, the grade and the pin
== mail.ticket.first
- A ticket case | A ticket case, when you're ready. It's on the Works board. Harder than the others. Take your time.
== ticket.card
- Ticket case: {machine} {shows}
== ticket.wrong
- Not yet. Next week.
== ticket.solved
- Ticket solved. Calder's initials on it.
== works.grade.1
- Fault-finder
== works.grade.2
- Trusted fault-finder
== works.grade.3
- The ship's fault-finder
== works.ms.grade
- {grade}, Day {n}.
== works.pin
- your fault-finder pin

// ---- off shift: cabin touches (E3, 24t). The spots and the things you can put there.
== cabin.spot.rug
- Rug
== cabin.spot.lamp
- Desk lamp
== cabin.spot.shelf
- Shelf
== cabin.spot.plant
- Plant
== cabin.item.rug.woven
- a woven rug
== cabin.item.rug.stripe
- a striped rug
== cabin.item.lamp.plain
- a plain desk lamp
== cabin.item.plant.fern
- a fern from the garden
== cabin.item.plant.herb
- a pot of mint

// ---- star logging (E3, 24t): the observatory telescope, 20:00-23:30, one a night
== star.title
- Telescope · tonight's field
== star.pick
- Three marked points. One's new. Which?
== star.right
- Logged. That one's new. It's yours: {star}.
== star.wrong
- That one's on the charts already. Try again tomorrow night.
== star.name
- Wren {n}
== star.done
- One a night. The sky will keep.
== works.ms.stars
- Star logger

// ---- Step 4 stages (E1): rounds stage 2 and 3, hauling, the stocktake; team parts (E2)
== round.title.first
- Your first round, Deck {deck}
== round.last
- last looked {n} days ago
== round.last.never
- not looked at yet
== round.doorway
- From the doorway: {machine}, {word}.
== haul.tidy
- A tidy run.
== stock.count
- {shelf}: count what's there.
== stock.short
- {shelf} is short of {part}.
== stock.job
- Restock: {shelf}
== stock.fine
- {shelf}: all present.
== mail.team.parts
- Bring the parts | {job} tomorrow at {time}. {name} asks you to bring the parts from stores: {parts}.
== team.parts.late
- {name} fetched the parts. Ten minutes late. Nobody minds. Much.

// ---- M17 the lift roof (E3, 24s): Thursdays 15:30-16:30 from Day 18
== roof.held
- The lift is held for maintenance until 16:30. Stairs, please.
== roof.result
- The lift runs a little smoother.
== roof.resume
- You'd saved on the lift roof. You're back at the top deck.
